From 95d267f1fd36dbd929db5f512ed165a25619ff7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:04:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/36] hw/misc: em35x-ncp, the flintstone's EM357 radio as a
 chardev

The Display-3.4 carries an EM357 802.15.4 NCP on ECSPI3 (fdt@4
spidev_em35x), chip select on GPIO4_IO30, nRESET on GPIO2_IO00, nWAKE on
GPIO2_IO05 and nHOST_INT into GPIO2_IO04 (em35x-gpios). Model the SPI
slave and those lines, and put the other end on a chardev: MOSI bytes and
line levels out, queued MISO bytes and nHOST_INT in, two bytes a message.
With nothing queued the slave clocks 0xff, and with no model attached
the radio reads as absent, as before.
---
 hw/arm/Kconfig              |   1 +
 hw/arm/flintstone.c         |  29 +++++
 hw/misc/Kconfig             |   4 +
 hw/misc/em35x_ncp.c         | 219 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/misc/meson.build         |   1 +
 include/hw/misc/em35x_ncp.h |  18 +++
 6 files changed, 272 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/misc/em35x_ncp.c
 create mode 100644 include/hw/misc/em35x_ncp.h

